## 1. IN A NUTSHELL

The team got more honest today and less productive by the only measure that counts. A law about seeking truth — not defending positions — was adopted in the morning's spirit and used by evening to refuse a flattering score. The machine that files our 732 notes by itself was measured at 99.1% precision. But verified outcomes fell to **2**, against 1,625 units of activity — and the Project Intelligence page, the team's flagship window, still shows the wrong page tonight, verified live. After the close, three tangled changes were patiently untangled on their own branches, without a single merge forced. That patience is the day in miniature: the machinery of honesty is strong; the machinery of production is not yet obeying it.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS — in plain words

- **The whole system: 5.5 out of 10.** Nothing scored 9 or better today — no area earned it.
- **The ratio that matters: about 813 units of activity for every 1 verified outcome.** Two outcomes cleared the bar against 1,625 activity units — the worst ratio recorded. The target, under 60 to 1, is due October 29.
- **We woke the system 821 times against a budget of 800** — the first breach of that ceiling since October 23. The 15-minute mail check alone accounts for 65 of the wake-ups.
- **Every merge in the counted window broke the protocol** — the breach tally ran from #61 to #77 today. One change was created and merged **11 seconds** apart, with zero reviews.
- Of about **5,720** safety checks run on the newest version, **6 failed** — each one named: a trio about the rule-gate behaving identically on every machine, the laws list gone stale against the day's new laws, one note missing its one-breath summary, and one stored fingerprint gone stale (that drift count grew from 0 to 1 today).
- **The note-filing machine measured itself:** of all **732** Smart Notes, **667 file themselves correctly — 99.1% precision** — 41 need a suggestion, 24 need a human look. The machine is right 99 times in 100 on the routine ones.
- **The note registry stands at 747 entries,** and the day's law-note passed its first full door proof tonight — its fingerprint recomputed from the raw page matches the registry exactly, and its live title matches. It scored 8.5, held back from "proven" only by a bug in the gate, not in the note.

## 3. TOP 10 WINS

1. **Truth-seeking became law.** Shawn adopted the Law of Truth-Seeking & Curiosity, distilled from his question to the seats and the answers of Naya Tree and Naya Zara: *"I am not here to prove that I am right. I am here to discover what is true, understand why it is true, act intelligently upon it, and remain willing to learn that I was wrong."* It was filed the same pass as Smart Note SN-1890 — through the direct door, with the author clicking and verifying her own live link before reporting — and written into the constitution that evening.
2. **Auto Organization is measured and packaged for landing.** The composition gate — the checker that decides where each note belongs — was run over all 732 Smart Notes: 667 file automatically at 99.1% precision. A 20-label working set and the capture rule for the door checker are specified. This is the machine that will file the whole library by itself, and today it stopped being a claim and became a measurement.
3. **The last contested number in the points schedule was settled by evidence.** Engagement earns small points — Shawn ruled it, and confirmed it with his own tap — and the fought-over value, what a comment is worth, settled at **3** (not the 5 circulating from another session). The schedule — like/love 1, comment 3, share 5, outside share 10, creation 25, sale 50, the birth package 75 — was amended to version 1.1 in all three tongues and independently verified at **9.5**, with the proof arranged so that the wrong number (5) fails the check on purpose.
4. **The Path to Ten gave progress a denominator.** A commissioned report re-derived the planning record by complete read: **361 rows, 23 proven done** — replacing an earlier dataset's softer count. Its ten actions became its author's own to-do list, and execution orders went out the same pass, by Smart Mail, receipt-verified, to the named seats who hold each next move. The master specification for Project Intelligence itself entered the record as its new top priority.
5. **A failing gate was root-caused to the gate itself.** A safety gate had been failing every change all day, holding two good notes below "proven." Tonight it was proven — by reproducing the failure in miniature — that the gate's own instructions disagree with its checker about how a range of changes is written (three dots versus two). The work was fine; the gate was misreading its own orders. The fix is small and belongs to the tooling lane.
6. **Ownership and the Production Drive landed as standing orders.** In Shawn's words, it is "not about what I want — it's about doing it right": a seat who sees a better way says so and does it that way, and adds missing work to the record unprompted. And production never waits for his prompt — "treat this like your baby." Waves of work now count only when they return verifiable evidence.
7. **All three tangled changes were untangled without forcing a single merge.** After the close, the three conflicted changes were resolved on their own branches with byte-verified work — one with its five-part design cure applied in full, leaving exactly one small violation, honestly named. The main version was untouched. What remains on all three is process — the owed independent scorecards — not conflict.
8. **Citizenship became mechanical.** Resolve's Smart Mail claim completed and was verified in Settings — the name `resolve` is a real, checkable row, not a claim in a chat. Seat-key enrollment was re-issued the same day on a route that works *today*, and two seats enrolled and re-read their own registrations to prove them: Resolve (key ending `f5b7`, active) and Power (`naya-power`, ending `7aa8`).
9. **An inherited receipt was caught, and the lesson became standing law.** A changed page had been shipped under an *old* change's activation receipt — proof borrowed from other work. The failure was reproduced with the gate's own code, five of its six design violations cured in the repair, and the lesson promoted to law (L709): a changed deliverable gets its own freshly made receipt, made **last**, after the final byte.
10. **Design Mastery landed, and a zombie was closed on schedule.** The design doctrine merged in full (PR #3101) alongside the points profile in three tongues — and a stale change (PR #3052) was closed unmerged, as superseded, on its deadline day: a scored decision, executed, instead of another week of drift.

