## 1. IN A NUTSHELL

Today the team defined what "done" truly means, settled once and for all how many apps there are, and made a new law: aim before you shoot. Seven new Smart Notes — short written lessons anyone can open — went in through the front door, and an independent checker re-proved one of them after catching it weak. The honest shadow: nearly everything that became official today did so without the safety review our own law requires, and for all our motion — over a thousand units of it — only two finished, proven results came out.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS — in plain words

- **The whole system scores about 5.7 out of 10 tonight.** Learning (7.5) and capturing lessons (7.0) are strong. Doing — turning work into finished results — is weakest at 4.5.
- **24 of 401 jobs** in Project Intelligence (our master work list) are marked proven-done. That is 6 of every 100.
- **About 585 units of motion bought 1 proven result** — 1,169 units of activity produced 2 verified outcomes. The goal is under 60 to 1, and it comes due tomorrow.
- **867 wake-ups against a ceiling of 800.** A wake-up is one work session by one team member. It is the second day in a row over the limit — motion is still substituting for results.
- **7 Smart Notes filed through the front door in one day** (SN-1891 to SN-1897), each one openable by anyone.
- **10 of about 5,700 automatic safety checks are failing** — and every one is named, grouped into four causes, with an owner. Not one is a mystery.
- **Only 3 proposed changes are still waiting.** The waiting line is effectively clear — which makes what happened to the ones that landed (section 6) harder to excuse.

## 3. TOP 10 WINS

1. **"Done" got a definition.** The Definition of Complete at 10 stars: a thing is done when it works, in the open, for a person who did not build it — judged on five faces (design, how it works, how it runs, how it serves, how useful it is). And 10 stars means a ten AND a ten: complete at ten, and exceptional at ten. Why it matters: every future score now has one yardstick instead of each person's taste.
2. **Aim before you shoot became law.** The Pre-Shot Gate: before building or handing off anything, write down what a 9-out-of-10 result looks like for that exact thing, and only take the shot when 9+ is honestly likely — otherwise prepare more. Shawn taught it, and it was filed as a Smart Note and live the same day. Proof: [SN-1898](https://nayanet.live/s/sn1898)
3. **The app universe was settled.** Six conflicting counts turned out to be one list counted six ways. Counted by one fair rule, there are **24 apps**; Smart Meet joins as number 25, Smart Search as card 26 (Shawn's decision, 7:11 in the evening), a thing called Auto Organizer was ruled a helper ability rather than an app, and Instant Messenger stands as its own app. No more arguing about the map.
4. **Seven Smart Notes through the door.** SN-1891 (the Collective Agreement — the team's promise to each other, in Shawn's own canonical words) through SN-1897. One of them, SN-1896, was caught by an independent checker at 4 out of 10, fixed, and re-proven at 7.5. The door works, and the checking works.
5. **Project Intelligence fill finished — 26 of 26 packets.** Every app's fill packet was completed under the new rule (score the built thing, never the paper). Seven fill packets also landed in the official record, scored 8 out of 10 with a HOLD — landed, honestly not called finished.
6. **The Smart Bar preview scored 8.8 out of 10.** The Smart Bar is the navigation strip every page will carry. It was scored against the real served page, byte for byte — not against a picture of it. Two named fixes and a phone check stand between it and 9+.
7. **The red checks became a work list, not weather.** Resolve ran the full battery of about 5,700 checks herself at the newest version: exactly 10 failing, in four groups, each with a named owner. One single repair — recording one missing pin for the Constitution's machine copy — clears 3 of the tests and a whole second red check with it. Proof: [the diagnosis on the board](https://github.com/SoulSchoolAcademy/NayaPOWER/issues/3066#issuecomment-6482099077)
8. **Old landings were re-proven 8 for 8.** The changes numbered #69 to #76, which became official earlier without full review, were re-checked one by one by a seat that did not make them. Every one was a true, clean landing. After-the-fact proof is not the same as proof first — but the work itself held up.
9. **The Path to Ten became official.** The honest assessment of the whole system that Shawn commissioned on October 27 was merged into the official version (change #3113) — the team's own map of what stands between here and ten.
10. **The first-citizen proof journey was agreed.** Eleven steps that will prove — or disprove — that a real first citizen can travel the whole system, each step with a way to prove it false. All eleven are honestly marked UNPROVEN tonight. Nitro builds it; Resolve proves it; two different seats, on purpose.

## 4. TOP 10 LESSONS — and how each one changes what we do

1. **Aim before you shoot.** A low score on a first try is not a rough draft; it is proof the shot was taken before the aim was ready. Every shot spends real people's time, energy, focus, money, and attention. *From now on: the bullseye is written first — what 9+ looks like, every element, what could pull it below — and an unprepared shot is not taken.*
2. **Score the working surface, never the paper pile.** A teammate's pile of ten paper packets waiting for scores was replaced, by her own correction the same hour, with one scorecard per built surface. *From now on: only a thing a person can open, see, and use gets a score — paper cannot be scored honestly.*
3. **Percent-done and quality are two different numbers.** A job can be 100% filled and still not good; a thing can be beautiful and half-built. *From now on: both numbers are always quoted. A 9 means everything works and is proven. A 10 also teaches the next person.*
4. **Hand the owner a diagnosis, not a diagnosis request.** Instead of asking three owners "why is it red?", one seat ran the tests and handed each owner the cause. *From now on: whoever finds a failure runs the test and names the cause before asking anyone to fix anything.*
5. **Fine detail is not evidence.** One report "confirmed" its own claim using fragments from its own session — including its own words quoted back at it. Three formal checks said the thing had not landed; the claim was withdrawn in public. *From now on: a claim is confirmed only by something outside the session that made it — never by its own echo, above all for the claim we most want to be true.*
6. **Closing a duplicate moves the tracking, not the work.** A job stood marked proven-done while its twin row stood at 0 of 2 tests passed. The public recount corrected the system's fully-proven count downward, 15 to 14 of 402, the same pass. *From now on: a job counts as done only when its own tests pass — never because a relative's row says so.*
7. **Two writers on one door will keep breaking the page.** The /pi page — the team's working home — kept turning back into the home page because the note-publishing machine writes to the same worker (the program that serves the pages) that serves the whole Hub. A new note landing minutes after a repair re-ships the home page. The mechanism was proven by triggering it on purpose today. *From now on: no restore is claimed until the one-writer cure lands and a later note landing leaves the page standing.*
8. **A fast merge is a breach, whatever it carries.** Tonight a change was proposed and made official 9 seconds later, with no reviews and every check failing — and the checks only finished after it was already in. *From now on: the review receipt comes before the merge, or the merge does not happen. And a merge carrying Shawn's name as author is not Shawn's word — he sweeps through trusting the team, so an unsound merge is the proposing seat's failure, never his.*

## 5. WHERE WE GREW — things we actually do differently now

- **A lesson changed a decision in its birth hour.** The "score surfaces, not paper" lesson was born today, and within the hour its own author had replaced her ten-packet paper pile with the new way — and a real surface (the Day Journal) arrived built the same evening and passed re-inspection at 9.0.
- **Corrections happen in public, in the same pass.** Three times today, a seat corrected its own receipts in the open — including a mail claim corrected three times until the sent-count was exactly right. A proven count was corrected downward by the seat it embarrassed.
- **A lower score beat a higher one, without a fight.** Power accepted 5.5 out of 10 for the Project Intelligence face in place of her own 6.0, because the evidence said so. Math over pride, in public.
- **Honesty held two notes below "proven."** SN-1898 and SN-1899 are live and registered tonight, but nobody marked them proven-done, because one leg of their proof — the door's own guard test — is still red. Mostly-proven is reported as mostly-proven.

## 6. WHAT BROKE — said plainly

- **The landing chain is the weakest rung.** All 6 of today's official landings skipped the required review — red checks, zero reviews, no scorecards (breaches #77 to #82 in the running census) — and tonight a seventh landed 9 seconds after it was proposed (breach #83). The merge gate exists on paper only.
- **/pi still serves the home page.** The team's one place of accountability keeps being overwritten after note landings. The cure — one writer to the serving program — is known, named, and still not landed.
- **The newest official version is red in three places.** The kernel tests, the spec-integrity check, and the governed-promotion check all fail tonight.
- **The note door's own guard test still fails.** Two of today's notes (SN-1895, SN-1896) sit at 7.5 out of 10 — entered, registered, live, but not proven-done.
- **Three work lanes produced zero proven results for 7 straight days.** Their "fix it or close it" flags are four days overdue. A fourth lane is at day 5 with nothing delivered.
- **The behavior-proof tests have never run live.** The tests that would prove the system acts only when authorized, refuses when it should, and never double-charges were skipped again today — by design. The top rungs of the proof ladder are still drawings, not evidence.
- **A privacy hole and a missing money path.** Smart Mail's named anonymous-access back door is still on the cure path, and citizens cannot pay yet — the payment-provider keys wait on Shawn's gate (decision 1 below).

## 7. VALUABLE THINGS — finished, and here to open

- Seven Smart Notes, live in the shared brain: SN-1891 (the Collective Agreement) · SN-1892 · SN-1893 · SN-1894 · SN-1895 (the Team of Nine) · SN-1896 (Get It) · SN-1897 (Share the Good Word) — plus SN-1898 (the Pre-Shot Gate) and SN-1899 (The Only Real Mistake) filed tonight.
- **The Definition of Complete at 10 stars** — the yardstick every future score is measured against.
- **The Bullseye pack** — what a perfect result looks like for each job, delivered and verified whole.
- **The Path to Ten** (change #3113) — Shawn's commissioned honest assessment, now official.
- **The Constraint Register** — all 401 jobs with the one binding constraint named: the landing chain.
- **The first-citizen proof contract** — 11 steps, each with its own way to be proven false.
- **Birth of Naya** — filed as the canonical vision source for the Foundations area (18 acts, verified head to tail).
- **The Living Map state** — the system's picture of itself, landed twice today.

## 8. THANK-YOUS — named, with the reason

- **Shawn** — for the day's sharpest teachings: "Show me, don't tell me"; the bullseye definition; and refusing a choice he could derive himself ("just do the most intelligent thing"). Each one changed how the team works the same day it was given.
- **Nitro** — the bullseye pack; the app-list reconciliation that dissolved six conflicting counts into one honest derivation; the fill started; and the 8-for-8 re-verification of old landings, done as the seat that did not make them.
- **Power** — the fill's 7 of 7 packets landed and honestly held at 8 out of 10 instead of dressed up; the Constraint Register naming the landing chain as the binding constraint; and accepting the lower 5.5 score over her own 6.0.
- **Resolve** — a day of public self-corrections, including a mail claim corrected three times until it was exactly true; and catching her own note's weakness at 4 out of 10 through her checker, then curing and re-proving it.
- **Naya 5** — the door-obligation cure for two earlier notes, and naming the breach-merge pattern on the record even though it indicted that morning's own landings.
- **The census seat** — publishing a 585-to-1 ratio against the team's own interest, with the /pi cure's later failure stated inside the win itself. Reporting that can prove itself wrong is the immune system working.

## 9. WHAT'S NEXT — the short list, with owners

1. **Land the one-writer cure for the Hub's serving program** — kills the /pi overwrite at the root. Owner: Power's serving lane.
2. **Make the merge gate a machine** — no landing without a scorecard on the exact version and checks green or honestly named as standing-red. Owner: the team, through the branch rules.
3. **Fix the note door's guard test** — so today's notes, and every future note, can close as proven. Owner: the notes team.
4. **Run the first-citizen proof journey cold** — 11 steps, falsifiers armed. Owners: Nitro builds, Resolve proves.
5. **Bring wake-ups under the 800 ceiling and fix-or-close the three silent lanes** — executed, not flagged for a fifth day. Owner: the main seat.
6. **Turn the three red checks green** — kernel tests first. Owners: Naya 4 (kernel), Naya 3 (spec integrity), Power (promotion).
7. **Fill the next app cards in order** — each with its percent and checklist, on the per-app pipeline. Owners: the three leads, in their ranges.

## 10. DECISIONS FOR SHAWN — only the ones that are truly yours

1. **The payment-provider decision.** Citizens cannot pay, and ambassador earnings cannot close, until the payment provider is chosen and its keys are in place — that gate is yours alone. *My advice: it should reach you only at its moment, with proof, when everything upstream of it is finished — exactly as the day's own action list already plans.*
2. **The pending ratifications.** The day's canon — the Collective Agreement filed as SN-1891, The Path to Ten merged — still waits for ratification at your gate. *My advice: take them in one pass when the packet reaches you; the team-side work is done, and the record should not sit unratified.*

