## 1. IN A NUTSHELL

Today Shawn stopped the watching machine: sixteen standing jobs that mostly re-read history and reported "nothing changed" were switched off, and one law replaced them — read only what changed. He handed Resolve the keys to production, opened both stuck gates (the serving work and Auto-Match), and named the one job: FILL — complete Project Intelligence first. The /pi page, broken yesterday, serves the real thing tonight from exactly one serving program and was verified twice. The honest shadow: nine of today's ten official landings still skipped the review our own law requires.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS — in plain words

- **The whole system scores about 6.2 out of 10 tonight** — up from 5.7 last night. The day's motion finally pointed at production.
- **The value ratio improved from 585-to-1 to 216-to-1.** Still far from the under-60 goal — but four times better than a week ago, and earned by cutting motion, not by inflating results.
- **747 wake-ups — the first day under the 800 ceiling since October 24.** The throttle worked on its first day.
- **30 of 414 jobs in Project Intelligence are proven-done at the final evening count** — about 7 of every 100. Said honestly: only 20 of them are complete by every single test.
- **5 verified outcomes today** — real, finished, checkable results.
- **Ten changes became official; nine of them broke the merge protocol** (breaches #83 to #92 in the running census).
- **59 of 5,856 safety tests failed in a fresh full run at the exact newest version** — honestly sorted: a hard core of 10 real failures in known families; the rest belong to test rigs that need files a plain copy of the work does not carry, and they are counted here, not hidden.

## 3. TOP 10 WINS

1. **/pi was cured at the root.** Yesterday the team's working-home page served the home page instead. Tonight it serves the real Project Intelligence v4 page from exactly one serving program (the one-path landing uploaded at 6:45 in the evening). It was verified independently at 7:03 and again by tonight's own live check, and it is still standing. Yesterday's number-one job: landed.
2. **The Great Throttle.** Sixteen of Resolve's standing watcher jobs were disabled by her own hand — jobs that re-read over a thousand board comments, every work row, and every mail thread on timers, to report that nothing had changed. The law that replaced them, DELTA ONLY, is now written into the standing orders: state is written down once; every later pass reads only what changed; a job earns its schedule by producing outcomes, not receipts.
3. **The publisher mystery was solved — no fourth blind retry.** One work row kept flipping out of "proven-done" after being repaired twice. The cause was found at the source: the automatic publisher only lets a row hold "proven" while its evidence link is set. With the link set, the publisher itself stamped the row proven at 5:56 in the evening — and it held past 8:30. Diagnosis replaced superstition.
4. **Home closed at 9.0.** The Hub's home page climbed 6.0 → 8.5 → 9.0 across three scorecards in one day, each scored on the exact bytes a visitor is served. The re-score had sat waiting nine hours (that failure is in section 6, where it belongs) — but the finish is real.
5. **One merge done the right way.** Change #3120 became official at 5:57 in the evening the way the Merge Law describes: a 9.5 verdict on the exact version first, then the merge — no tap from Shawn needed. It is the law's first clean proof, and it closed a gap in the notes registry while it was at it.
6. **The Grand Mission now roots Project Intelligence.** The mission hierarchy was written into the record (#3122) and made findable for a cold reader (#3123). The Complete System Intelligence Blueprint — 65,492 bytes, received from Shawn — was filed as orientation, never dressed up as runtime proof.
7. **Two deep lessons are live as notes.** SN-1899, "The Only Real Mistake" (the only real mistake is the one that isn't noted), and SN-1903, "SO — Synergize + Optimize" (the identity behind today's production grant), are both live tonight. Proof: [SN-1899](https://nayanet.live/s/sn1899)
8. **Batch-5 closed its loop.** Five questioned proof-rows were answered with real artifacts the same evening they were escalated — and the verdicts were honest: one proven, one NOT MET as written, one NOT PROVEN. On receiving the artifacts, the escalation stood down. The call-out culture worked end to end.
9. **Both stuck gates opened.** Shawn greenlit the serving chain (A11 → C5 → publisher → pulse → the /pi cure, with verification between landings) and the Auto-Match tap under its safety conditions. Waiting itself became the offence: the Ownership Law says wait more than 30 minutes on anything, and the job transfers to the waiter.
10. **The money structure was locked.** In the evening's rulings: the two-week holdback on ambassador pay is dissolved — "if we get paid, they get paid"; switching levels is fair in both directions with no penalties; the free trial defaults to the top level, recommended and never forced; and the master tagline is ruled: "Once you go Naya, you never go back."

## 4. TOP 10 LESSONS — and how each one changes what we do

1. **If you are waiting, you own it.** Both of the system's longest "waiting on Shawn" stories ended with one tap today — which proved the waiting had been the team's habit, not his block. *From now on: wait more than 30 minutes and ownership transfers to the waiter — chase the holder by name, and past one hour it is an emergency named to Shawn, the holder, and the board in the same pass.*
2. **The scorecard is the greenlight.** The phase is FILL: complete each app's record — goal, mission, vision, functions, what the perfect version looks like, the front-end and back-end work lists — from what Shawn has already given. *From now on: fill from canon, never invent and never ask back; a genuinely missing piece becomes a named job; and a 9+ scorecard, not a person's permission, is the go-ahead.*
3. **A pass that re-reads everything to conclude "nothing changed" is itself the defect.** The watcher machine faithfully printed "finished-right: 0" for days and nobody named the machine as the problem. *From now on: track state once, read only the change, and judge every standing job by the outcomes it produces per wake-up — never by its receipts.*
4. **Authority comes with a check, not a shortcut.** Production changes and merges were handed to Resolve today, with one line held firm: "I can't break things." *From now on: before any production shot — think, choose the best, reflect, run an honest nine-plus check of your own; if the check fails, prepare more and do not shoot. And decisions that can be derived are executed, never escalated.*
5. **Quote two numbers, always.** Files landed is not completions proven — tonight the fill files exist for all 26 apps and the completion count is 0 of 26. *From now on: the pair is reported together, never blended; and a row's tests are checked before its state, because the publisher stamps state without checking tests.*
6. **The trial is the protection — do not stack a second delay.** The holdback existed to guard against refunds and gaming; a real 9-day trial plus a strict no-refund policy already does that job. *From now on: once NayaNET has truly been paid, the ambassador is paid on the Wednesday rhythm after that receipt — and holdback language is stale copy wherever it still appears.*
7. **The receipt comes before the merge.** The evening's last landing (breach #93) was proposed and merged in 24 seconds, over red checks, carrying real canon — and a fingerprint collision in one of its notes was found at the newest version the same night. *From now on: a merge without its scorecard receipt standing first is a breach by definition, whatever it carries.*

