## 1. IN A NUTSHELL

Today the system learned its own definition. Shawn distilled what Naya is — one app with four doors, where everything else is a feature, not a separate app — and ordered every seat to feed the network daily: note what you learn the moment you learn it, and file a report every day. The team wrote it all down faithfully and even repaired eight days of missing reports. But the day's other record is hard: eight proposals were merged into the main line against the merge law — the count of those breaches rose from 121 to 129 in one day — and the daily count of verified outcomes, measured honestly, was zero.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS

- **Verified outcomes: 0** — the first zero day since counting began (yesterday: 1). The evening's merges do not count: every one broke the merge law, and a landing outside the law is not a verified outcome. (Daily value census, board #3066 comment 6613802476.)
- **Merges into the main line: 8 — all 8 were breaches** (#122–#129: PRs #3156, #3157, #3158, #3160, #3161, #3162, #3163, #3164). Content mostly good; the gate never happened. Retro-checks now owed: 23 (#107–#129).
