2. **Eight days of missing reports, cured at the cause.** The filed report series had silently stopped on October 23 while the nightly job kept "succeeding" by sending PDFs to chat. Tonight the backfill landed: Daily editions October 24 → November 2, the missing October 25 learning event, and the Weekly/Monthly shelf — 15 new files, none edited after the fact (PR #3164; merge = breach #129). And the job itself was fixed: from tonight, every run files its edition into the system the same night, or declares itself INCOMPLETE. *This report is that cure's first test.*
3. **One App, reconciled by first claim.** Two seats taught the same doctrine in parallel — Nitro's SN-0874 and Resolve's SN-2044. First claim stood: SN-0874 is the one true note, the duplicate was closed unmerged, its number returned to the pool, and the losing seat cured the winner's missing index entry herself (PR #3161; merge = breach #124). *Why it matters:* the no-duplicates rule worked end-to-end, in the open, the same evening it was tested.
