## 1. IN A NUTSHELL

Today the system found its operating system and its mirror. Shawn locked the five algorithms of Naya World, named the goal — maximum efficiency at producing verified, valuable work — and asked every seat to look in the mirror; Resolve's answer named the root plainly: witness mode, checking and reporting instead of finishing. Real finishes did land: the registry cure for 21 notes was verified 21 of 21 after landing, seven of last night's breach landings were retro-verified byte by byte, and Smart Mail's door opened on the official domain after a two-month block. But the day's landings mostly arrived the wrong way — twelve proposals swept onto the main line in one burst with no scorecard on record — and the one number that matters most, finished-and-proven Project Intelligence rows, did not move at all.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS

- **Verified outcomes: 9** — seven breach landings from November 3 retro-verified byte by byte (board comment 6635415609), the 21-note registry cure verified 21 of 21 after it landed (comment 6645888030), and one citizen surface newly proven live: Smart Mail on nayanet.app, identity restored and re-read as Resolve/resolve in check after check through the evening. Project Intelligence rows reaching done-and-proven today: **0** — the count is 30 of 502, flat for the seventy-third straight lock-in check.
- **Merges: 13 proposals merged — 12 onto the main line, 1 into a stacked branch — and the breach count rose 130 → 140 in one day.** Team Verity numbered the evening burst #131–#139 and the late restore #140. Retro-verifications now owed: 25 at the settled 23:10Z accounting, plus #140.
- **Checks on the whole system (the kernel battery, run fresh tonight on the exact tip): 5,643 passed, 78 failed, 19 skipped, 6 set aside as known-flaky (xfailed), 1 error** — failures jumped from 19 yesterday to 78 today. The new damage is concentrated where the day's import landed: the note index (8 failures), cold retrieval (14), and the activation checklist's pins (25) — the machine underneath got worse while the doctrine grew.
- **The waiting pile: flat at 1,253 items, past its 200th straight hour** (hourly accountability, board #3066). Nothing finished from the pile again today.
