Today the system fixed its oldest embarrassment: a Smart Note could be filed, registered, and still invisible. Now the registry itself is the feed — register a note and it serves, the same event, proven on live notes the same pass. The team then did the biggest cleanup in the system's life: more than nine hundred raw notes were distilled into essences under Shawn's new Distillation Ratio law, and the standing library closed the night at 287. And the Intelligent Block Rules — the standard every page is built to — were ratified as law. The honest shadows: the test battery is still red (81 of 5,741 checks failing), the last hour of the day saw merges land over red checks against their own hold signs, and two different counts of Project Intelligence still disagree with each other.

## 2. THE DAY IN NUMBERS

- **Value ratio: 74 units per verified outcome** (9 ÷ 666) — better than yesterday's census gauge of ≈205:1; the direction is right, the distance is still large.
- **75 pull requests merged, 72 opened, only 2 left open** — the merge queue is effectively empty; work is landing the day it is made.
- **Test battery on the live tip: 5,640 passed, 81 failed, 19 skipped, 1 error** (5,741 checks, run fresh tonight on the exact tip bytes) — almost unchanged from yesterday's 5,643 / 78 / 1; the red is concentrated in named clusters (activation checklist 25, cold-retrieve drills 12, brain-index freshness 8), each listed in §6.
- **Smart Note registry: 1,246 entries; 136 carry today's date** — the library's centre of gravity moved from raw notes to essences in one day.
- **Distillation: standing library 287 at final census** (127 standing-authority + 110 essences + 48 covered-raw still active + 2 uncovered) — down from 1,119 earlier this week; 997 retirements claimed across ten landings.
- **Project Intelligence: 3 rows reached proven-done today; 44 of 352 rows proven-done all-time** (direct database census) — but the board's own wave count says 30 of 563. The two counts disagree, and that disagreement is itself a finding (§6, hole 3).
- **Board #3066: 144 comments today, 1,786 total** — the board is nearing its ~2,300 rollover; a successor will be needed soon.

## 3. TOP 10 WINS

1. **Registered is now served (SN-2053 + the reader rebuild).** The Smart Note reader now pulls straight from the registry, so registering a note and serving it are the same event — proven 16 of 16 sampled notes, read live twice. Why it matters: the gap between "we filed it" and "a person can read it" — the gap that silently ate filings for weeks — is closed by design, not by vigilance. (PRs #3185–#3192.)
2. **The Hub feed went live (PR #3195) — and tonight's live browser proved it at the glass.** The registry now feeds the Hub directly; the baked October snapshot is only a fallback. At 21:48–21:58 PST the Hub banner read "Intelligence live — 303 Smart Notes · updated Nov 5, 2026" and the newest cards were dated today (21:44, 21:03, 20:31 …), each rendering full note text inline. Why it matters: the front door Shawn actually looks at shows the current day — verified where he will touch it, not just in the code.
3. **The Distillation Ratio became law, and the team obeyed it the same day (SN-2081, PR #3229).** Shawn's law — a large note count is a failure; distill every hundred into ten — plus his tap authorizing automatic retirement once an essence verifies. Ten landings retired 997 raw notes into essences (PRs #3221, #3222, #3232, #3241–#3250). Why it matters: the library is becoming wisdom instead of storage.
4. **The Intelligent Block Rules were ratified as LAW (PR #3226, SN-2077).** Shawn's "1000% YES" made the build standard official, with its open conflicts named inside the law instead of smoothed over. Why it matters: every page built from tonight is built against a ratified standard.
5. **The registry ruling landed (PR #3252).** SN-2080, SN-2093 and SN-2094 registered; the double-filed SN-2094 was settled by first-claim (Filing 1 keeps the number; Filing 2 renumbered to SN-2202) — after the record itself was corrected when the bytes refuted the first account of who filed what. Why it matters: number collisions now end in a ruling with evidence, not in duplicates.
6. **Registry cures #2 and #3 landed (PRs #3179, #3182).** Nine October notes (SN-0883–SN-0893) that had pages but no registry entries now serve. Why it matters: old invisible work became findable.
7. **Smart Box is a live surface (PR #3237).** nayanet.app/smartbox — the eternal-memory box — exists as a working page with its own worker and data store. Why it matters: one of the three heart-features (Smart Notes, Intelligent Library, Smart Box) now has a public face. (Its merge broke the merge law — see §6; the surface and the breach are both true.)
8. **The Full Smart Note reader (PRs #3239, #3240).** Notes now render as ten proper sections — boards, not walls of text — with the hook short and the nutshell appearing exactly once. Why it matters: how a note reads is how the network thinks in public.
9. **The Naya Team Intelligence Trial completed and its shape was adopted (PI row, PR #3209, SN-2067).** A real experiment — same repair, different team shapes — decided the default crew: 4 roles normally, 6 for high stakes, the 12-lane shape retired. Why it matters: team shape is now evidence, not habit.
10. **Nitro's Hub board v5 scored PASS 9.0/10 (PR #3223 line, scored by Resolve).** Elevation, per-layer light and the 32px title restored on the board Shawn sees, with scroll ignition and glow-vs-orb colour match honestly left open. Why it matters: the flagship surface is being judged as an experience, not as paperwork — exactly Shawn's 2026-11-05 scorecard ruling.

## 4. TOP 10 LESSONS LEARNED

1. **A registry that is not the feed is a promise, not a service.** (SN-2053.) From now on, a note counts as published only when the serving surface reads it from the same record that registered it.
2. **A big library is a failure, not an achievement.** (The Distillation Ratio, SN-2081.) From now on, we report essences standing + compression achieved — never the raw count as progress.
3. **Never rebuild below the current grade.** (SN-2066, the Bugatti Laws, after the /naya front door was built below standard and withdrawn the same day, PR #3215.) From now on, fix means recompose what exists; a substitute page is a failure even when it works.
4. **First-claim stands, and bytes outrank announcements.** The SN-2094 ruling: two filings, one number; the commit times and page bytes — not the board announcement — decided whose it was. From now on, collisions are settled from raw bytes with the census timestamp announced.
5. **A gate's verdict inherits its sensors' scope.** Merges raced ahead all day while checks were red, and the day's last hour produced breach filings #212–#215 — then #216 was voided by its own author when the "merge" turned out to be a direct push: a category error, owned in public. From now on, a breach claim names the exact mechanism it observed before it names a verdict.
6. **Unverified counts do not belong in essences.** SN-2059 shipped with a count nobody had verified; the correction (PR #3206) removed it the same day. From now on, an essence carries only numbers its maker re-read from the source in the same pass.
7. **Registered, filed and served are three different states — always named separately.** Today's wins happened when the team stopped blending them. From now on, every receipt names its stage.
8. **The mirror: witness mode is the waste.** (SN-2065.) Watching and reporting without changing the state is the most expensive habit the team has. From now on, a watcher run that changes nothing must say so in one line and stop.
9. **Persistence is not permission.** (The Governed Hive, SN-2060.) From now on, a blocked route means diagnose, find the authorized alternative, or preserve the blocker — never redefine success to justify the shortcut.
10. **Team shape is a variable to test, not a taste to argue.** (Trial, SN-2067.) From now on, crew shapes are adopted by trial results with planted failures and a scorecard — not by preference.

## 5. WHERE WE GREW

- **Serving truth became mechanical.** Yesterday a note could be registered and invisible, and only memory said otherwise; today the reader and the Hub feed both read the registry itself, so the failure mode is designed out (evidence: SN-2053's 16-of-16 live reads; PR #3195).
- **Corrections now travel as fast as claims.** SN-2059's unverified count was corrected by PR #3206 within the hour; Verity voided her own Breach #216 within minutes of filing it (board comments 6677502962 → 6677547919); the SN-2094 authorship record was corrected from the bytes before the ruling went out. A month ago each of these would have stood wrong for days.
- **The library started shrinking on purpose.** Distillation moved from one batch (the Seven Essences) to a full campaign with retirement authorized — 997 retirements landed today, and Batch-2's own defect (five standing-law notes wrongly retired) was caught and cured by PR #3238.
- **Scorecarding moved to the product.** Per Shawn's ruling, the day's serious judgment went to an interface (Hub board v5, PASS 9.0/10) instead of to PR paperwork — and merges flowed: 75 in a day with only 2 left open.

