### What is it saying, in the simplest words?

The team built machines to do the squeezing, the checking, and the filing, and Shawn made the rules simple and clear: build everything side by side, let everybody earn, close each day the next morning, and count a note only when a person can open it where people actually live. All of that is real progress, and none of it has yet turned into a single new proven outcome — the proven column stayed at 30 all day and night, the short links still send people to a dead address, and sixty-seven new notes still cannot be found in the team's own memory. The day says: the tools are ready and the rules are clear — now use them to finish things a second pair of eyes can prove, starting with the doors people actually click.

